Package: REGATTA
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Eco-Geographic Assignment Through Taxonomic Adjustment
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Eldridge", "Wisely", email = "ewisely@ucsd.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ella", "Crotty", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Summary-table format designed by Ella Crotty.")
    )
Author: Eldridge Wisely [aut, cre],
    Ella Crotty [ctb] (Summary-table format designed by Ella Crotty.)
Maintainer: Eldridge Wisely <ewisely@ucsd.edu>
Description: Correct off-target species assignments in eDNA metabarcoding
    results by reconciling classifier output against a regional species
    checklist, without manual curation and while preserving as much
    taxonomic specificity as possible. The package optionally also
    reconciles two classifier outputs (e.g. against a global vs. a
    locally-curated reference database) using percent identity to pick
    the better-supported call and falling back to the lowest common
    ancestor when the two disagree.
